node_modules/
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Rival lockfiles. pnpm is pinned by `packageManager` so corepack resolves the version the Dockerfile
# builds with, and pnpm-lock.yaml is the only tree that is ever installed — CI uses --frozen-lockfile
# and the image builds from it.
#
# `.claude/settings.json` also denies `npm install`, and that rule protects EXACTLY ONE PARTICIPANT:
# the assistant reading it. A person who types the command sees nothing, and a lockfile that lands is
# committable, believed, and quietly describes a tree nothing installs. The deny is a convenience;
# this is the part that holds regardless of who ran what.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
bun.lockb

test-results/
playwright-report/
# Where the Playwright MCP browser writes snapshots, screenshots and any file it is handed. Tool
# output, and its allowed roots are inside the repo — so without this it lands in `git status`.
.playwright-mcp/

# Agent skills, vendored by `npx autoskills` and reconstructible from it — skills-lock.json is the
# committed record. The symlinks under .claude/skills point into .agents, so both go together: a
# committed symlink into an ignored directory dangles on clone, and on a host without symlink
# support git checks it out as a text file holding the path, which is worse than absent.
.agents/
.claude/skills/*

# Hand-written and versioned, unlike everything else under .claude/skills. Any project skill added
# later needs its own negation here — the rule above is what keeps a vendored symlink out.
!.claude/skills/smoke/

# gentle-ai's skill registry. Machine-specific — it records absolute paths from the host that
# generated it.
.atl/
